Subject: Leave the Pulsar collector and lz4-java out of the slim jar
Origin: DHI-internal (slim distribution scope)
Description: Exclude zipkin-collector-pulsar and lz4-java from the slim repackage.
 Upstream documents the slim distribution as in-memory or Elasticsearch storage
 with HTTP or gRPC span collectors. The Pulsar collector added in 3.5.0 never
 joined the slim excludes, so the slim jar still carries pulsar-client with its
 Bouncy Castle, OpenTelemetry and validation-api dependencies. lz4-java moved
 from org.lz4 to at.yawk.lz4, which the existing org.lz4 group exclusion misses;
 only the Kafka collector, already excluded from slim, uses it.
Base-Tree: git https://github.com/openzipkin/zipkin.git b2b0c98acf20944766bb1365de04b3316da83078
Regenerate: `git -C zipkin diff -- zipkin-server/pom.xml` (on the pristine tree, with only this exclusion edited)
Verify: test tests/zipkin_slim_test.go::TestZipkinSlimDEB
Forwarded: no (not reported upstream yet)
Drop-When: upstream >= 3.7.0 (if that release excludes the Pulsar collector and lz4-java from slim)
CVE: CVE-2026-106449
CVE: CVE-2026-106450
CVE: CVE-2026-106451
CVE: CVE-2026-106452
